{
  "name": "death_flop",
  "duration": 1.4,
  "loop": false,
  "channel": "BASE",
  "_note": "Ends held at the pose of the last key. body rot ends at exactly +12, the stated body limit, so it sits ON the bound without clamping - inclusive bounds are the tested behaviour. Every other bone stays inside its limit. Keeping the fallen penguin inside the host viewport is the RENDERER's job (constraints.dashboard_boundary); this layer does not clip to a viewport it cannot see. Sign convention: +rot is CLOCKWISE ON SCREEN, because the canvas origin is top-left and +y points DOWN.",
